
Phase 4: Generate the Correct SAS Token
Your PowerShell script likely used an Account Key or a broad SAS. The browser needs a specific, secure Container SAS.
In your Storage Account, go to Data storage > Containers on the left menu.
Click on the specific container that holds your folders and ZIP files.
At the top of the container page, click Shared access tokens (or "Generate SAS").
Configure the token:
Allowed permissions: Check Read and List. (Do not check Write or Delete unless absolutely necessary).
Start and expiry date/time: Set an expiry date in the future (e.g., 1 year from now).
Allowed protocols: HTTPS only.
Click Generate SAS token and URL.
Copy the entire Blob service SAS URL (it will start with https://... and end with ?sp=rl&st=...).
